Below are the principal columns you will need, together with their “potential usage” and the typical conditions that will be applied later on.

• PATENTS_USPTO.USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS.PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS  
  – "pat_no":   patent number, used to link to MATCH for its publication number  
  – "appl_id":  application identifier, later joined to PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS to pick the first (earliest) publication of that application  
  – "claim_no": claim number, required in final answer  
  – "word_ct":  word count per claim (stored as text → cast to number); used for ranking  
  – "ind_flg":  ‘1’ = independent claim (filter criterion)

• PATENTS_USPTO.USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS.MATCH  
  – "pat_no":            patent number to match with PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS."pat_no"  
  – "publication_number": full DOCDB‐style publication number to be returned

• PATENTS_USPTO.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS  
  – "publication_number": join to MATCH."publication_number"  
  – "publication_date":   used to pick the very first publication of each "appl_id"  
  – "application_number_formatted": convenient normalised application id to match to PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS."appl_id" (by simple cast or string comparison)

Key conditions that will be used
  • PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS."ind_flg" = '1'  
  • We will CAST/TRY_TO_NUMBER("word_ct") for ordering  
  • Earliest publication per application: use MIN("publication_date") in a window or sub‑query

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Ten example Snowflake SQL snippets (all limited to 20 rows) move from basic inspection to the final composite query.  
Every column name is enclosed in double quotes; comments start with “--”.

```sql
--1. Quick look at claim statistics and the independent‑claim flag
SELECT
  "pat_no",
  "claim_no",
  "ind_flg",
  "word_ct",
  "appl_id"
FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2. Independent claims only
SELECT
  "pat_no",
  "claim_no",
  "word_ct",
  "appl_id"
FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS"
WHERE "ind_flg" = '1'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3. Top independent claims by raw (string) word count
SELECT
  "pat_no",
  "claim_no",
  TRY_TO_NUMBER("word_ct") AS "word_ct_num",
  "appl_id"
FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS"
WHERE "ind_flg" = '1'
ORDER BY TRY_TO_NUMBER("word_ct") DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4. Attach the publication number by joining to MATCH on patent number
SELECT
  pcs."pat_no",
  m."publication_number",
  pcs."claim_no",
  TRY_TO_NUMBER(pcs."word_ct") AS "word_ct_num",
  pcs."appl_id"
FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS"  pcs
JOIN "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."MATCH"               m
  ON m."pat_no" = pcs."pat_no"
WHERE pcs."ind_flg" = '1'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5. Add publication date & application number from PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
SELECT
  pcs."pat_no",
  pub."publication_number",
  pub."publication_date",
  pub."application_number_formatted",
  pcs."claim_no",
  TRY_TO_NUMBER(pcs."word_ct") AS "word_ct_num"
FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS"  pcs
JOIN "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."MATCH"               m
       ON m."pat_no" = pcs."pat_no"
JOIN "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS"                 pub
       ON pub."publication_number" = m."publication_number"
WHERE pcs."ind_flg" = '1'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6. Earliest publication date per application (sub‑query)
SELECT
  pub."application_number_formatted",
  MIN(pub."publication_date") AS "earliest_pub_date"
FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" pub
GROUP BY pub."application_number_formatted"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7. Combine earliest date info with publications table
SELECT
  pub."publication_number",
  pub."application_number_formatted",
  pub."publication_date"
FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" pub
JOIN (
    SELECT
      "application_number_formatted",
      MIN("publication_date") AS "earliest_pub_date"
    FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS"
    GROUP BY "application_number_formatted"
) first_pub
  ON first_pub."application_number_formatted" = pub."application_number_formatted"
 AND first_pub."earliest_pub_date" = pub."publication_date"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8. Earliest publication linked back to independent claims
WITH first_pub AS (
  SELECT
    pub."application_number_formatted",
    MIN(pub."publication_date") AS "earliest_pub_date"
  FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" pub
  GROUP BY pub."application_number_formatted"
)
SELECT
  pcs."pat_no",
  pub."publication_number",
  pcs."claim_no",
  TRY_TO_NUMBER(pcs."word_ct") AS "word_ct_num",
  pcs."appl_id"
FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS"  pcs
JOIN "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."MATCH"               m
       ON m."pat_no" = pcs."pat_no"
JOIN "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS"                 pub
       ON pub."publication_number" = m."publication_number"
JOIN first_pub fp
       ON fp."application_number_formatted" = pub."application_number_formatted"
      AND fp."earliest_pub_date" = pub."publication_date"
WHERE pcs."ind_flg" = '1'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--9. Rank by word count (still limited to 20) after ensuring earliest publication
WITH first_pub AS (
  SELECT
    pub."application_number_formatted",
    MIN(pub."publication_date") AS "earliest_pub_date"
  FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" pub
  GROUP BY pub."application_number_formatted"
)
SELECT
  pub."publication_number",
  pcs."appl_id"                     AS "application_id",
  pcs."claim_no",
  TRY_TO_NUMBER(pcs."word_ct")      AS "word_count"
FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS"  pcs
JOIN "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."MATCH"               m
       ON m."pat_no" = pcs."pat_no"
JOIN "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS"                 pub
       ON pub."publication_number" = m."publication_number"
JOIN first_pub fp
       ON fp."application_number_formatted" = pub."application_number_formatted"
      AND fp."earliest_pub_date" = pub."publication_date"
WHERE pcs."ind_flg" = '1'
ORDER BY TRY_TO_NUMBER(pcs."word_ct") DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Final form: top‑100 longest independent patent claims with the first publication of each application
WITH first_pub AS (   --earliest pub per application
  SELECT
    pub."application_number_formatted",
    MIN(pub."publication_date") AS "earliest_pub_date"
  FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS" pub
  GROUP BY pub."application_number_formatted"
),
joined AS (           --link independent‑claim stats → publication numbers → earliest pubs
  SELECT
    pub."publication_number",
    pcs."appl_id"                     AS "application_id",
    pcs."claim_no",
    TRY_TO_NUMBER(pcs."word_ct")      AS "word_count"
  FROM "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."PATENT_CLAIMS_STATS"  pcs
  JOIN "PATENTS_USPTO"."USPTO_OCE_CLAIMS"."MATCH"               m
         ON m."pat_no" = pcs."pat_no"
  JOIN "PATENTS_USPTO"."PATENTS"."PUBLICATIONS"                 pub
         ON pub."publication_number" = m."publication_number"
  JOIN first_pub fp
         ON fp."application_number_formatted" = pub."application_number_formatted"
        AND fp."earliest_pub_date" = pub."publication_date"
  WHERE pcs."ind_flg" = '1'
)
SELECT
  "publication_number",
  "application_id",
  "claim_no",
  "word_count"
FROM joined
ORDER BY "word_count" DESC
LIMIT 100;
```

Each successive query builds understanding, leading to the complete solution that returns (publication_number, application_id, claim_no, word_count) for the 100 longest independent claims, taken only from the earliest publication tied to each application.
